# Phase 5: Internet Deployment (Going Live)

This plan outlines the complete process of taking your Kudeja Trading platform from your local computer (`localhost`) and publishing it to the live internet so that anyone in Ethiopia and beyond can access it.

## 1. What You Need Before We Start

Before we begin the technical setup, you will need a few things ready:

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **A Domain Name**: You need to decide on your web address (e.g., `kudeja.com` or `kudejatrading.et`). I can help you set this up on a provider like **Namecheap** or **Google Domains**.
> 
> **A Hosting Account**: We need "Cloud" space. For your specific tech stack (React + Node + Postgres), I recommend **Render.com** or **Railway.app**. They are very reliable and offer free/cheap tiers to start.
> 
> **Email App Password**: Ensure you have that 16-character Google App Password ready for the Email Service we built in Phase 2.

---

## 2. The Deployment Process (Steps)

The deployment happens in three main stages:

### A. The Database (The Brain)
- Currently, your data is stored on your PC. We will move this to a **Cloud Database** (like Neon.tech or Render Postgres).
- We will "Export" your local data and "Import" it into the cloud so you don't lose any products or categories.

### B. The Backend (The Heart)
- We will upload your `kudeja-backend` folder to a server.
- We will configure your **Environment Variables** (`.env`) on the server so the password and database links stay hidden from the public.
- The server will give us a "Production URL" (e.g., `api.kudeja.com`).

### C. The Frontend (The Face)
- We will run a command to "Build" your React app. This compresses the code into a small, fast package.
- We will upload this to a host like **Vercel** or **Render**.
- Finally, we will point your **Domain Name** (`kudeja.com`) to this file so users see your beautiful design when they type the URL.

---

## 3. Security & Production Checklist

Before the site goes live, we must ensure:
* [ ] **SSL (HTTPS)**: Ensuring the "Green Lock" appears in the browser so customer data is encrypted.
* [ ] **CORS Settings**: Restricting your backend so only *your* frontend can talk to it (protects against hackers).
* [ ] **Error Logging**: Setting up a tool to tell us if the server crashes while you're sleeping.

---

## 4. Open Questions for You

> [!WARNING]
> **Budget**: Most cloud services start for free, but for a professional business with many images, you might need a small monthly budget (approx. $7-$20 USD/month total). Is this within your expectations?
>
> **Global vs Local**: Do you want your site to be hosted on servers physically close to Ethiopia for speed, or is a global provider (USA/Europe) okay?

Does this process make sense? If you are ready, our first step will be choosing the Hosting Provider!
